            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 57-year-old male patient, admitted on 28/10/2008 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were performed to exclude concurrent infection or other complications. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy with good clinical response. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. He was discharged on 29/10/2008 in a stable condition with optimised inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. I recommend close follow-up and reinforcement of inhaler technique and smoking cessation advice. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
